st-of-moravia">Jobst of Moravia</a> is elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1479</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-olomouc">Peace of Olomouc</a> leaves <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus of Hungary</a> for his lifetime</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1579</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravian-church">Unity of the Brethren</a> begins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kralice-bible">Kralice Bible</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1628</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renewed-land-ordinance">Renewed Land Ordinance</a> makes the crown hereditary and curbs the Moravian estates</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1866</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregor-mendel">Gregor Mendel</a> publishes his plant experiments made in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1918</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> becomes a land of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a></span></li></ol>
